### 💡 Why You’re Seeing This
The Jasmine/Karma test files Angular auto‑generates try to `new` your directive classes with no arguments,  
but your directives require constructor arguments like:

```ts
constructor(private el: ElementRef, private renderer: Renderer2)
```

and the mock `Renderer2` object you attempted to provide isn't the correct type according to TypeScript’s strict typing.

---

## 🟢 The Fastest Fix (Recommended)

✅ **Just delete or ignore these spec files**, since they are *only used for testing*.  

These files are:

```
src/app/login/Directives/blink.spec.ts
src/app/login/Directives/highlight.spec.ts
src/app/login/Directives/rotate.spec.ts
src/app/login/Directives/scale.spec.ts
src/app/login/Directives/shadow.spec.ts
```

You can delete them safely with **no impact on your Angular app**.

```bash
# PowerShell delete
del src\app\login\Directives\*.spec.ts
```

> Once deleted, re‑run:  
> ```bash
> ng serve --open
> ```

🎯 App will compile and run with **zero TS errors**.

